e space as {site} x {residue} x\n{word position} x {p_bit} and says *\"close every cell in ONE diff\"* -- it then honoured {site} for\n`M_MASK7` (adding BOTH the LDM and STM BIT2 rows) and did NOT honour it for `p_bit`, adding only\n`THUMB_PUSH_COLD_DATA_P2`.  Three cells of a two-by-two.\n\n*Missable for a structural reason worth keeping: the load-side cell CANNOT be closed by copying the\npush row -- the probe's only p_bit=1 caller is Thumb PUSH, so closing {load}x{p_bit=1} needs a NEW\nINSTRUCTION WORD (LDMIB/LDMDB), not a new base.*\n\nTHE BRIEF'S OWN CANDIDATE `& ~15` **DIES** (M_MASK15 30/32), and `M_MASK1` reproduced\n`killtable_20260911e` exactly (29/32) -- so the rig rebuilds and the probe discriminates.\n\nIT ALSO FOUND `THUMB_PUSH_COLD_DATA_P2` IS THE **SOLE CARRIER** OF THE WHOLE p_bit AXIS (an L3\nshape), reads through the freshly-repaired `read_mem32`, and asserts ONE half where its sibling\n`ARM_STM_COLD_DATA_BIT2` asserts two -- adding `w1 == 0` is free.\n\nRECOMMENDED CLOSURE, one diff: LDM IB/DA/DB/S at residue 2 with DATA oracles, plus\n`LDMIA r0!,{r1,r2}` from +2 -- **one leg, three assertions, kills M_POPW_WEAK AND M_NPMASK and\ncloses the w_bit x residue-2 and reg-list-length axes together**; mirror on the store side.  And\nthe repair owes its own pass: passes A, B and C each found a breach."
