tools/pipeline/ledger.json:25430:     "note": "PASS 2 -- VERDICT: DO NOT RATIFY -- 566 KB, and the highest-yield seat of pass 2. *** REFUTED THIS ROUND'S OWN 'MEASURED REACHABLE' CLAIM FOR THE BULK ARM, and I verified it before accepting: wdc__read() has exactly ONE caller and it sits AFTER wdc_new_command_reset(), so the ring is EMPTY on every real invocation. The prefilled state the rows build is a FUNCTION state, not a guest route -- 'the fixture built a function state, not a product route'. *** The comment is corrected in place; the hunk stays as DEFENSIVE, licensed by the caller invariant being unwritten anywhere else. Also traced the new `break`: wdc__read() returns no residual, sets no error, and reaches the common tail setting int_assert -- so a refusal presents to the guest as a COMPLETE transfer. Named M_bulk_ge (`>` -> `>=`) as a predicted survivor WITH its killing row, and argued for deleting the now-unreachable post-hoc check whose comment the fix makes false.",
tools/pipeline/ledger.json-25431-     "outcome": "UPHELD",
