tools/pipeline/ledger.json:27711:     "note": "*** A SEAT OUTCOME THE TAXONOMY DOES NOT NAME: INVESTIGATION WITHOUT CONCLUSION. ***\n\n462 KB, 7240 lines, 98% novel, and NO VERDICT ANYWHERE.  The answer TERMINATES INSIDE A FILE\nIT WAS QUOTING -- its last line is the closing brace of a scratch generator of mine that it\nhad opened to read.  It did real work: 1111 lines of grep/file output across the repo.  It\nsimply never landed.\n\nIT IS NONE OF THE RECORDED CLASSES.  No quota text, so not a WALL.  98% novel, so not the\necho-only shape.  Substantial output, so not the minimax-style stall.  A CLI seat, so not the\ndeepseek thinking-burn (`done_reason: length`).  Not a refused connection.\n\n*** AND seat_verdicts.py FILED IT AS 'answered, NO VERDICT LINE (format miss)'. ***  That is\nthe daemon case's conflation again: a seat that produced NO ANSWER recorded as a seat with\nbad FORMATTING.  Scoring it 'answered' credits a verdict that does not exist, and this panel\nwould read 6 answered when the honest count is 5 plus one unfinished.\n\nA CHECKABLE SIGNATURE EXISTS AND IS CHEAP: does the answer END INSIDE A QUOTED FILE OR CODE\nBLOCK rather than with a sentence?  A finished answer ends in prose.  This one ends in `}`.\nThat is a different question from 'is there a verdict line', which is a FORMAT question --\nand the two are being answered by one check.\n\nNOT GENERALISED FROM ONE INSTANCE, deliberately: the same seat produced a real verdict with a\nreal finding on #484's pass 2 (566 KB) and a substantive answer on #485 (2.2 MB, the landisk\nunmapped-write finding at its tail).  So this is not 'codex is broken'.  It is one firing\nthat ran out mid-investigation, and the value of recording it is the SIGNATURE, not the\nseat.\n\nFILED, not fixed: teaching seat_verdicts.py the ends-inside-a-quote discriminator is a change\nto the tool every panel runs, and it owes two negative controls -- prove it fires on this\nfile, and prove it does NOT fire on #484's codex answer, which ends in prose and has a\nverdict.  That is its own small round."
tools/pipeline/ledger.json-27712-    },
